<title>AUSTRIA: IRAN SAYS NOT SATISFIED WITH OIL PRICES.</title>
<headline>IRAN SAYS NOT SATISFIED WITH OIL PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian oil minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh said on Monday he was not satisfied with oil prices and said that OPEC should take steps to stop quota violations.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not satisfied,&quot; he told reporters when asked about current oil prices.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have lost a lot of the price since January. The price depends on our action in the market,&quot; Aghazadeh said.</p>
<p>The price of North Sea Brent Blend has fallen from around $25 per barrel earlier this year to just below $18 now.</p>
<p>Asked what OPEC should do about the oil price, Aghazadeh said: &quot;We have overproduction. (We should) stop violations&quot;.</p>
<p>OPEC's output ceiling is 25.033 million barrels per day (bpd) but the group is currently producing around 2.0 million bpd above that level.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
